  "display_title": "The Serpent's Den",
  "description": "Edwin Rocher and Leila Garwen grew up as childhood friends, but everything shifted the moment they became adults. When Edwin quietly asked, “Teach me how to touch myself,” Leila gave in to the request, thinking it would end there. Instead, he became addicted to the filthy pleasure Edwin fed him, and Leila found himself unable to escape the boy he once thought he knew so well. One night, Leila stumbles upon a creature with green eyes soaking in Edwin’s bath...a monster wearing the face he trusted most. In that moment, he realized he never truly understood what Edwin is, or what he wants. Caught between fear, desire, and the monstrous truth, Leila enters a den of corruption where escape is impossible and surrender may be the only path left.\n\n(Source: Lezhin US)",
